@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`

-- National-Civic Service Law, 5774-2014, s 36 (validity), and what it does to the temporary text of
-- National Insurance Law s 348(e). Row IL-34, priority 1: BACKLOG IL-05's fork 05-Q7.
-- Quotations: `src:N` is line N of the National Insurance Law's deposited text, `ext:[civic] N` is line N of
-- the Civic Service Law's (../../../national-civic-service-law-5774-2014/registers/source-bundle/), both
-- generated by tools/srcquote.py and tools/extquote.py.
--
-- WHAT THE TEXTS SAY.
--   Civic Service Law s 36(a): the Law stands in force until 31.8.2026.
--   Civic Service Law s 36(b): the Law goes on applying after that day to one who began service before it,
--     and to the operating body he serves with, until his service ends.
--   NII s 348(e), temporary text: for as long as the Civic Service Law stands (and, after the expiry, for
--     one who began service before it), one serving in national-civic service is treated as having the
--     Schedule K item 3 minimum when he has no income or less than it.
--
-- WHAT THE DEPOSITED TEXTS CANNOT SAY. Whether a LATER Act moved the 31.8.2026 day. The Civic Service Law's
-- consolidation is the Wikisource page as of 2026-04-01 and lists Amendment No. 9 as its last; today is after
-- 31.8.2026, so an Amendment 10 would be the next Act in the line 30.6.2025 > 15.11.2025 > 31.3.2026 > 31.8.2026
-- that row IL-05 records. NEEDS A SOURCE: the Knesset database / Reshumot for any amendment of that Law
-- after 2026-04-01. Until then every question whose answer turns on the day is declined by name; every question
-- whose answer is the same wherever the day falls is answered (NOTES.md, forks C1 to C3).

§ `National-Civic Service Law s 36 and National Insurance Law s 348(e)`

§§ `s 36(a) and (b) of the National-Civic Service Law`

-- ext:[civic] 329 | סעיף 36 – תוקף [תיקון: תשע״ו, תשפ״ג, תשפ״ד, תשפ״ה, תשפ״ו, תשפ״ו־2]
-- ext:[civic] 330 | (א) חוק זה יעמוד בתוקף עד יום ”י“ח באלול התשפ״ו (31 באוגוסט 2026) (בסעיף זה – מועד הפקיעה).
-- ext:[civic] 331 | (ב) הוראות חוק זה יוסיפו לחול אף לאחר מועד הפקיעה על מי שהחל את שירותו לפי חוק זה לפני מועד הפקיעה ועל הגוף המפעיל שאצלו הוא משרת, עד תום שירותו.

-- The day as the deposited text states it.
@ref National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) (civic line 330); Wikisource revision 3002360, 2026-04-01
GIVETH A DATE
`National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) — the expiry day, as the deposited text states it` MEANS
    YMD 2026 8 31

-- The Law's own commencement is not in the deposited text: s 37(b) and (d) call it "the commencement day"
-- and s 37(f) speaks of a service begun in the period "from the commencement day until 30 June 2014", so
-- the Law began on or before that day. A day up to and including 30.6.2014 is declined.
@ref National-Civic Service Law s 37(f) (civic line 339); NOTES.md, section "Needs a source"
GIVETH A DATE
`National-Civic Service Law — the last day on which its commencement day may fall, from s 37(f)` MEANS
    YMD 2014 6 30

@ref National-Civic Service Law s 37(f) (civic line 339)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the commencement day of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited text` MEANS
    REFUSE "the commencement day of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited text, and it falls on or before 30 June 2014"

@ref National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) (civic line 330); NOTES.md fork C2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 36(a) says the Law stands until a day and does not say whether that day itself is a day of the Law` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 36(a) says the Law stands until a day and does not say whether that day itself is a day of the Law"

@ref National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) (civic line 330); NOTES.md fork C1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts` MEANS
    REFUSE "whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts, and the answer turns on it"

@ref NOTES.md fork C1
GIVEN one IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the answer if` one `and` other `agree, or else the readings differ` MEANS
    IF one EQUALS other THEN one ELSE `whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts`

-- A day far beyond any expiry: "moved to some later day", the end of the range a declined reading stands for.
@ref NOTES.md fork C1
GIVETH A DATE
`a day later than any the question could turn on` MEANS
    YMD 2999 12 31

§§ `Whether the Law is in force on a day`

-- "The Law shall stand in force until [the day]": for a day before it, yes; after it, no; on it, fork C2.
@ref National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) (civic line 330); NOTES.md fork C2
GIVEN `the day`    IS A DATE
      `the expiry` IS A DATE
      r            IS A `A reading of the expiry day itself`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Law is in force on` `the day` `if it stands until` `the expiry` `, reading the expiry day as` r MEANS
    BRANCH IF Day `the day` LESS THAN    Day `the expiry` THEN TRUE
           IF Day `the day` GREATER THAN Day `the expiry` THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER r
               WHEN `the Law is in force through the expiry day`   THEN TRUE
               WHEN `the Law ends at the start of the expiry day`  THEN FALSE
               WHEN `the expiry day itself is declined`            THEN `s 36(a) says the Law stands until a day and does not say whether that day itself is a day of the Law`

-- Put at the readings. A day up to the last possible commencement is declined first.
@ref National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) (civic line 330), s 37(f); NOTES.md forks C1, C2
GIVEN d  IS A DATE
      rs IS A `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` d `, reading its expiry as` rs MEANS
    IF Day d AT MOST Day (`National-Civic Service Law — the last day on which its commencement day may fall, from s 37(f)`)
    THEN `the commencement day of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited text`
    ELSE
        CONSIDER rs's `for whether the expiry was moved`
        WHEN `the expiry stays as the deposited text states it`      THEN `in force if it stands until` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) — the expiry day, as the deposited text states it`)
        WHEN `a later Act moved the expiry to` x                      THEN `in force if it stands until` x
        WHEN `whether a later Act moved the expiry is declined`       THEN
            `the answer if` (`in force if it stands until` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) — the expiry day, as the deposited text states it`))
                `and` (`in force if it stands until` (`a day later than any the question could turn on`)) `agree, or else the readings differ`
    WHERE
        `in force if it stands until` e MEANS `the Law is in force on` d `if it stands until` e `, reading the expiry day as` (rs's `for the expiry day itself`)

-- The same, at the switch: every reading declined.
@ref NOTES.md, Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law`
`National-Civic Service Law s 36 — the readings this row takes where the texts do not decide` MEANS
    `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law` WITH
        `for whether the expiry was moved`   IS `whether a later Act moved the expiry is declined`
        `for the expiry day itself`          IS `the expiry day itself is declined`
        `for what ends the temporary text`   IS `what ends the temporary text is declined`

@ref National-Civic Service Law s 36(a)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` d MEANS
    `the National-Civic Service Law is in force on` d `, reading its expiry as` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36 — the readings this row takes where the texts do not decide`)

§§ `s 36(b): the Law goes on applying to one who began before the expiry`

-- "The provisions of this Law shall go on applying, even after the expiry date, to one who began his service
-- under this Law before the expiry date, and to the operating body with which he serves, until the end of his
-- service." Before: strictly (a person who began on the expiry day itself did not begin before it; the same
-- reading row IL-05 takes, its fork F8). `serving` is a fact: the person is serving on the day asked about.
@ref National-Civic Service Law s 36(b) (civic line 331)
GIVEN s   IS A DATE
      d   IS A DATE
      serving IS A BOOLEAN
      rs  IS A `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(b) — the Law applies to one who began service on` s `, serving on the day` d `is` serving `, reading its expiry as` rs MEANS
    IF NOT serving
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE
        CONSIDER rs's `for whether the expiry was moved`
        WHEN `the expiry stays as the deposited text states it`      THEN `applies if it stands until` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) — the expiry day, as the deposited text states it`)
        WHEN `a later Act moved the expiry to` x                      THEN `applies if it stands until` x
        WHEN `whether a later Act moved the expiry is declined`       THEN
            -- the answer never falls as the day moves later, so TRUE at the printed day is TRUE at every day
            IF `applies if it stands until` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) — the expiry day, as the deposited text states it`)
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts`
    WHERE
        `applies if it stands until` e MEANS
                (Day s LESS THAN Day e)
            OR  `the Law is in force on` d `if it stands until` e `, reading the expiry day as` (rs's `for the expiry day itself`)

§§ `The temporary text of National Insurance Law s 348(e)`

-- src:3769 | [note: (הוראת שעה עד מועד הפקיעה של חוק שירות לאומי־אזרחי, התשע״ד–2014, ביום 31.8.2026, חלה גם על מי שהתחיל את שירותו לפני המועד האמור גם אחרי המועד האמור עד שייסים את שירותו):] מתנדב בשירות לאומי או בהתנדבות קהילתית, משרת בשירות לאומי–אזרחי, תלמיד במוסד תורני או בישיבה או מי שמשרת בשירות אזרחי כהגדרתו בסעיף 6(א) לחוק דחיית שירות לתלמידי ישיבות שתורתם אומנותם, התשס״ב–2002, שאין לו הכנסה או שהכנסתו אינה מגיעה לסכום המזערי האמור בפרט 3 בלוח י״א, יראו כאילו הכנסתם היתה הסכום המזערי האמור.
-- src:173 | ”משרת בשירות לאומי–אזרחי“ – [note: (הוראת שעה עד מועד הפקיעה של חוק שירות לאומי–אזרחי, התשע״ד–2014, ביום 31.8.2026, חלה גם על מי שהתחיל את שירותו לפני המועד האמור גם אחרי המועד האמור עד שייסים את שירותו):] מי שמשרת בשירות לאומי–אזרחי כהגדרתו בחוק שירות לאומי–אזרחי, התשע״ד–2014;

-- The temporary text is "until the expiry date of the Civic Service Law ... which applies also to one who
-- began service before that date, also after that date, until he completes his service". Fork C3: whether
-- it ends with that Law whenever that is, or on 31.8.2026. Put as the days the question is asked at:
-- one end, or two where the reading is declined.
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), editors' note to the temporary text (source line 3769); NOTES.md forks C1 and C3
GIVEN rs IS A `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law`
GIVETH A `The ends the temporary text of section 348(e) may have`
`the ends the temporary text of section 348(e) may have, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` rs MEANS
    CONSIDER rs's `for what ends the temporary text`
    WHEN `the temporary text ends with the Civic Service Law, whenever that is` THEN `The ends the temporary text of section 348(e) may have` WITH `the first` IS follows, `the second` IS follows
    WHEN `the temporary text ends on 31.8.2026 whatever happens to the Civic Service Law` THEN `The ends the temporary text of section 348(e) may have` WITH `the first` IS stays, `the second` IS stays
    WHEN `what ends the temporary text is declined` THEN `The ends the temporary text of section 348(e) may have` WITH `the first` IS follows, `the second` IS stays
    WHERE
        stays   MEANS `it ends on` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) — the expiry day, as the deposited text states it`)
        follows MEANS
            CONSIDER rs's `for whether the expiry was moved`
            WHEN `the expiry stays as the deposited text states it`   THEN stays
            WHEN `a later Act moved the expiry to` x                   THEN `it ends on` x
            WHEN `whether a later Act moved the expiry is declined`    THEN `it ends on the printed day or on a later one`

-- The first and last day of a span of whole months.
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN sp IS A `A span of whole months of one tax year`
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the span` sp MEANS
    YMD (sp's `the tax year`) (sp's `the first month`) 1

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN sp IS A `A span of whole months of one tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of the span, as a day count` sp MEANS
    IF sp's `the last month` EQUALS 12
    THEN Day (YMD ((sp's `the tax year`) PLUS 1) 1 1) MINUS 1
    ELSE Day (YMD (sp's `the tax year`) ((sp's `the last month`) PLUS 1) 1) MINUS 1

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), temporary text (source line 3769)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the temporary text of section 348(e) ends inside this span, and the person began national-civic service on or after the day it ends` MEANS
    REFUSE "the temporary text of section 348(e) ends inside this span, and the person began national-civic service on or after the day it ends"

-- Does the temporary text reach the span, if it ends on the day E?  Yes if the span ends by E; yes if the person
-- began before E (strictly); no if the span begins after E; otherwise the span straddles E, which (e) does not
-- apportion, and it is declined (row IL-05's reading).
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), temporary text (source line 3769)
GIVEN began IS A DATE
      sp    IS A `A span of whole months of one tax year`
      e     IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the temporary text reaches a person who began on` began `, for the span` sp `, if it ends on` e MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the last day of the span, as a day count` sp AT MOST Day e                  THEN TRUE
           IF Day began LESS THAN Day e                                                      THEN TRUE
           IF Day (`the first day of the span` sp) GREATER THAN Day e                       THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE `the temporary text of section 348(e) ends inside this span, and the person began national-civic service on or after the day it ends`

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), temporary text (source line 3769); NOTES.md forks C1, C3
GIVEN began IS A DATE
      sp    IS A `A span of whole months of one tax year`
      `the end` IS A `The days on which the temporary text of section 348(e) may end`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the temporary text reaches a person who began on` began `, for the span` sp `, if` `the end` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the end`
    WHEN `it ends on` e THEN `the temporary text reaches a person who began on` began `, for the span` sp `, if it ends on` e
    WHEN `it ends on the printed day or on a later one` THEN
        -- never falls as the end moves later: TRUE at the printed day is TRUE at every later day
        IF `the temporary text reaches a person who began on` began `, for the span` sp `, if it ends on` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36(a) — the expiry day, as the deposited text states it`)
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE `whether a later Act moved the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law is not in the deposited texts`

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), temporary text (source line 3769); s 1 "משרת בשירות לאומי–אזרחי" (source line 173)
GIVEN began IS A DATE
      sp    IS A `A span of whole months of one tax year`
      rs    IS A `The readings of the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` began `, for the span` sp `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` rs MEANS
    `the answer if` (`the temporary text reaches a person who began on` began `, for the span` sp `, if` (ends's `the first`))
        `and` (`the temporary text reaches a person who began on` began `, for the span` sp `, if` (ends's `the second`)) `agree, or else the readings differ`
    WHERE
        ends MEANS `the ends the temporary text of section 348(e) may have, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` rs

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), temporary text (source line 3769)
GIVEN began IS A DATE
      sp    IS A `A span of whole months of one tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` began `, for the span` sp MEANS
    `s 348(e) — the temporary text reaches one serving in national-civic service who began on` began `, for the span` sp `, reading the Civic Service Law's expiry as` (`National-Civic Service Law s 36 — the readings this row takes where the texts do not decide`)
